# Support don't care bit 'x' in the mode bits definition of OpenFPGA Architecture Language

- Source URL: https://github.com/lnis-uofu/OpenFPGA/issues/2161

**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**
When integrating custom blocks containing fracturable mode selection bits, it happens that a pb_type in a operating mode only requires to update partial mode-selection bits. 
For example, a multiplier with the following fracturable operating modes:

- Single 18x18 - Combinational
- Single 18x18 with input registers
- Dual 9x9 - Combinational
- Dual 9x9 with input registers, each 9x9 can operate separately.

In the case, when users try to map two multiplier primitives

- 9x9 combinational
- 9x9 with input register

into a logic block (assume each logic block contains only 1 fracturable multiplier)

We want VPR to select the best location for each primitive in the logic block.
Therefore, the mode selection bits for each primitive 9x9 with input register should require to update only part of the mode-selection bits of its physical pb_type.

```
<pb_type name="mult_16" physical_mode_name="mult_16x16"/>
<!-- The first bit switches between 9x9 and 18x18 mode -->
<!-- The second bit switches between enable/disable input register for the first 9x9 -->
<!-- The third bit switches between enable/disable input register for the second 9x9 -->
<pb_type name="mult_16[mult_16x16].mult_16x16_slice.mult_16x16" circuit_model_name="frac_mult_16x16" mode_bits="100"/>
<!-- The first 9x9 with register should only alter the second bit -->
<pb_type name="mult_16[mult_8x8].mult_8x8_slice.mult_8x8_regin_0" physical_pb_type_name="mult_16[mult_16x16].mult_16x16_slice.mult_16x16" mode_bits="01x"/>
<!-- The first 9x9 with register should only alter the second bit -->
<pb_type name="mult_16[mult_8x8].mult_8x8_slice.mult_8x8_comb_0" physical_pb_type_name="mult_16[mult_16x16].mult_16x16_slice.mult_16x16" mode_bits="00x"/>
<!-- The second 9x9 with register should only alter the third bit -->
<pb_type name="mult_16[mult_8x8].mult_8x8_slice.mult_8x8_regin_1" physical_pb_type_name="mult_16[mult_16x16].mult_16x16_slice.mult_16x16" mode_bits="0x1"/>
<!-- The second 9x9 with register should only alter the third bit -->
<pb_type name="mult_16[mult_8x8].mult_8x8_slice.mult_8x8_comb_1" physical_pb_type_name="mult_16[mult_16x16].mult_16x16_slice.mult_16x16" mode_bits="0x0"/>
```

**Describe the solution you'd like**


The mode bits should support the don't care bit ``x``.
When a bit is defined as 'x', the mode-selection bit of operating pb_type will not update the corresponding bit of its physical pb_type.
As such, partial mode bit mapping is achieved.
**Only the operating modes allow don't care bits**
